        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 8,
        "line_end": 8,
        "exact_text": "1. `network`, `station`: ID of the network and the measuring station\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_86c0857947c65f6d2fb9",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 9,
        "exact_text": "2. `channel`: channel name e.g. BHE\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_4f0bf9ed78c91a4eece4",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 10,
        "line_end": 10,
        "exact_text": "3. `longitude`,`latitude`: location of the station in degrees\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_410d4a4f6635fc66888b",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 11,
        "line_end": 11,
        "exact_text": "4. `elevation_m`: elevation of the station in meters\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_28f48e616185eb005481",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 12,
        "line_end": 13,
        "exact_text": "5. `response`: instrument sensitivity at this station\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_f2507f5793cc2aef9ca8",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 17,
        "line_end": 17,
        "exact_text": "1. Load the waveform and station data.\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_3dee35df1df6db81e52a",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "SUPPORT",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 18,
        "line_end": 18,
        "exact_text": "2. Pick the P and S waves in the earthquake traces with deep learning models available in the SeisBench library.\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_d6fb48b003c557938719",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 19,
        "line_end": 19,
        "exact_text": "3. Using the picking results and the station data to find the common earthquake events. In particular, you should produce a unique list of events with their timestamp.\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_58fcbd54ab0fc9138e81",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/earthquake-phase-association/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 20,
        "line_end": 21,
        "exact_text": "4. Write the results to `/root/results.csv`. Each row should represent one earthquake event. There must be a column `time`, indicating the time of the event in ISO format without timezone. Other columns may be present, but won't be used for evaluation.\n\n",
        "source_sha256": "93226fabc6076d540a125924863474736e9b1bec77dafe3ffcb7d64898043f48",
        "extraction_rule": "commonmark_list_item"
      }
    }
  ],
